---
source: crates/cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: stdout(&out)
---
Browse and edit the open tasks in a full-screen terminal UI

Usage: tasq ui [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --profile <NAME>
          Apply the `[profile.<NAME>]` block of the config files (also TASQ_PROFILE)

      --config <FILE>
          Use FILE instead of the global config file (also TASQ_CONFIG)

      --set <KEY=VALUE>
          Override one config key, e.g. --set store.notebook=work. Repeatable

      --json
          Print machine-readable JSON (every document carries "schema": 1)

      --color <WHEN>
          When to colour the output: auto (only on a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour when stdout is a terminal and NO_COLOR is unset
          - always: Always emit colour escapes
          - never:  Never emit colour escapes
          
          [default: auto]

      --no-color
          Never colour the output (same as --color never)

      --no-pager
          Print long output directly instead of through the pager (`ui.pager`)

  -v, --verbose...
          Show more detail (bookkeeping output, resolved paths). Repeatable

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

The list is the grouped view of `tasq`, with the selected task's detail
beside it (or, below 100 columns, behind Tab). Keys: j/k move, g/G first
and last, / filter (text matches titles; #word is a status, tag or
priority as for `tasq <word>`), s status, p priority, l log a note, d mark
done (with an optional final note), e open the file in $VISUAL or $EDITOR,
Enter open a work session (`tasq pick`), S run the sources (`tasq sync`),
r reload, ? help, q quit. Edits are the same operations as `tasq set`,
`log` and `done`. Group colours follow [ui.colors] (status name, or
`no-status`); NO_COLOR or --color never gives a monochrome UI.
